repository-code: https://github.com/pa1aash/oxide-vacancy-descriptors
abstract: >-
  An open framework for predicting neutral oxygen-vacancy formation energies in non-magnetic oxides with MEGNet
  graph networks that read the pristine crystal structure alone (S) or the structure together with
  density-functional electronic descriptors of the host (D, and D* after a wider hyperparameter search), and a
  staged network (P) that first predicts the descriptors from the structure, with random-forest and two-parameter
  physics baselines. The repository holds the package, the analysis code, the job specifications, the splits and
  the stored result records with the per-site predictions of every run, and re-derives the numbers, tables and
  figures of the associated study from those records without retraining and without a GPU. All DFT data come from
  the oxygen-vacancy database of Kumagai et al. (CC BY 4.0). Code is released under MIT, data and results under
  CC BY 4.0.
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - oxygen vacancy
  - defect formation energy
  - non-magnetic oxides
  - density functional theory
  - graph neural network
  - MEGNet
  - electronic descriptors
  - learning curve
  - reproducibility
